      "headings": [
        "# Mechanotransduction and Piezo2 Channels in Somatic Sensing",
        "## Abstract",
        "## Physiological Mechanisms",
        "### Piezo2 Channel Structure",
        "### Proprioceptive Role",
        "### Interoceptive Role",
        "### Fascial Mechanosensation",
        "## Relevance to Internal Movement Arts",
        "## Guardian Interface Links"
      ],
      "summary": "Mechanotransduction converts mechanical forces into electrochemical signals within biological tissues. Piezo2 is the primary mechanically activated ion channel responsible for proprioception, light touch, and interoception in mammals. Understanding Piezo2 provides a molecular foundation for somatic awareness and the physiological basis of embodied practices such as Tai Chi and Qigong."
